IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 2: s 5(2)(a) to (e), (3) to (7) and (9): what a licence granted under s 5(1) may require, and what it costs.
-- (s 5(1), (2) opening, (8) and (10) are in sgta-s3-5-privilege-licensing.l4.)
-- The seat is the licensee's: what may I be required to do, what must I pay, and what can I not get back.

§ `s 5(2): conditions a licence may include`

-- src:620 | (a) the licensee to enter into agreements or arrangements with
-- src:621 | any person, class of persons or another
-- src:622 | telecommunications licensee for —
-- src:624 | (i) the interconnection of, and access to,
-- src:625 | telecommunication systems;
-- src:627 | (ii) the sharing of installation or plant used for
-- src:628 | telecommunications belonging to any
-- src:629 | telecommunication licensee; and
-- src:631 | (iii) such other purpose as may be specified in the licence,
-- src:633 | (a) and on such terms and conditions as may be agreed to by
-- src:634 | the licensee and such other persons or licensees or, in
-- src:635 | default of agreement, as may be determined by the
-- src:636 | Authority;
@ref s 5(2)(a) (src:620-636)
GIVEN `the licence includes a condition requiring the licensee to enter into agreements or arrangements with a person, a class of persons or another telecommunications licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the interconnection of, and access to, telecommunication systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the sharing of installation or plant used for telecommunications belonging to a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is another purpose specified in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(a): the licensee is required to enter into the agreement or arrangement` MEANS
        `the licence includes a condition requiring the licensee to enter into agreements or arrangements with a person, a class of persons or another telecommunications licensee`
    AND (   `the purpose is the interconnection of, and access to, telecommunication systems`
         OR `the purpose is the sharing of installation or plant used for telecommunications belonging to a telecommunication licensee`
         OR `the purpose is another purpose specified in the licence`)

GIVEN `the licensee and the other persons or licensees have agreed terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`s 5(2)(a): the terms and conditions of the agreement or arrangement are` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the licensee and the other persons or licensees have agreed terms and conditions` THEN "as agreed by the licensee and the other persons or licensees"
           OTHERWISE "as determined by the Authority, in default of agreement"

-- src:638 | (b) the sharing and trading of radio frequency spectrum;
@ref s 5(2)(b) (src:638-638)
GIVEN `the licence includes a condition requiring the sharing and trading of radio frequency spectrum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(b): the licensee is required to share and trade radio frequency spectrum` MEANS
    `the licence includes a condition requiring the sharing and trading of radio frequency spectrum`

-- src:643 | (c) the licensee to comply with any direction given by the
-- src:644 | Authority as to such matters as are specified in the licence
-- src:645 | or are of a description so specified;
@ref s 5(2)(c) (src:643-645)
GIVEN `the licence includes a condition requiring compliance with directions of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is as to a matter specified in the licence or of a description so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(c): the licensee must comply with the Authority's direction` MEANS
    `the licence includes a condition requiring compliance with directions of the Authority` AND `the direction is as to a matter specified in the licence or of a description so specified`

-- src:647 | (d) the licensee to comply with codes of practice and standards
-- src:648 | of performance that are applicable to the licensee; and
@ref s 5(2)(d) (src:647-648)
GIVEN `the licence includes a condition requiring compliance with codes of practice and standards of performance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code of practice or standard of performance is applicable to the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(d): the licensee must comply with the code of practice or standard of performance` MEANS
    `the licence includes a condition requiring compliance with codes of practice and standards of performance` AND `the code of practice or standard of performance is applicable to the licensee`

-- src:650 | (e) the licensee to do, or not to do, such things as are specified
-- src:651 | in the licence or are of a description so specified.
@ref s 5(2)(e) (src:650-651)
GIVEN `the licence includes a condition requiring the licensee to do or not to do things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is specified in the licence or is of a description so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(e): the licensee must do, or must not do, the thing` MEANS
    `the licence includes a condition requiring the licensee to do or not to do things` AND `the thing is specified in the licence or is of a description so specified`

§ `s 5(3) to (7), (9): fees, refund, validity, the Minister's direction`

-- src:655 | (3) The grant of a licence under subsection (1) is subject to the
-- src:656 | payment to the Authority of such fees for the grant of the licence as
-- src:657 | may be prescribed.
@ref s 5(3) (src:655-657)
GIVEN `the prescribed fee for the grant of the licence has been paid to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(3): the grant of the licence is effective as to payment` MEANS
    `the prescribed fee for the grant of the licence has been paid to the Authority`

-- src:661 | (4) A licensee must also pay to the Authority such other fees for the
-- src:662 | licence, or such periodic fees for the duration of the licence, or
-- src:663 | both —
-- src:665 | (a) as may be prescribed; or
-- src:667 | (b) if not prescribed, as may be specified by the Authority in
-- src:668 | the licence conditions.
@ref s 5(4) (src:661-668)
GIVEN `the fee is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee is specified by the Authority in the licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(4): the licensee must pay this other or periodic fee to the Authority` MEANS
    `the fee is prescribed` OR ((NOT `the fee is prescribed`) AND `the fee is specified by the Authority in the licence conditions`)

-- src:672 | (5) Any fees payable under subsection (3) or (4) in respect of a
-- src:673 | licence —
-- src:675 | (a) need not bear any relationship to the cost of granting or
-- src:676 | administering the licence; and
@ref s 5(5)(a) (src:672-676)
GIVEN `the fee is payable under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(5)(a): the fee must bear a relationship to the cost of granting or administering the licence` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:678 | (b) are recoverable by the Authority from the licensee as a debt
-- src:679 | due to the Authority.
@ref s 5(5)(b) (src:678-679)
GIVEN `the fee is payable under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(5)(b): the Authority may recover the fee from the licensee as a debt due to the Authority` MEANS
    `the fee is payable under subsection (3) or (4)`

-- src:683 | (6) A licensee is not entitled to the refund of any fee paid under
-- src:684 | subsection (3) or (4) if —
-- src:686 | (a) the licence is cancelled or suspended, or the period of the
-- src:687 | licence is reduced, under section 10; or
-- src:689 | (b) the licence is terminated at the request of the licensee.
@ref s 5(6) (src:683-689)
GIVEN `the licence is cancelled or suspended, or the period of the licence is reduced, under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is terminated at the request of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(6): the licensee is entitled to the refund of a fee paid under subsection (3) or (4)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the licence is cancelled or suspended, or the period of the licence is reduced, under section 10` OR `the licence is terminated at the request of the licensee`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:693 | (7) No person is to question whether the grant of a licence under
-- src:694 | subsection (1) was, or was not, effected with the consent of or in
-- src:696 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:697 | 15 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:699 | accordance with the terms of a general authority given by the
-- src:700 | Minister, and the validity of a licence granted under that subsection
-- src:701 | must not be impugned on the ground that it was granted neither with
-- src:702 | the consent of nor in accordance with the terms of a general authority
-- src:703 | given by the Minister.
@ref s 5(7) (src:693-703)
GIVEN `the licence was granted neither with the consent of the Minister nor in accordance with the terms of a general authority given by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(7): the validity of the licence may be impugned on the ground that it was granted without the Minister's consent` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:708 | (9) This section does not prevent the Minister from directing the
-- src:709 | Authority to grant a licence in any specific case.
@ref s 5(9) (src:708-709)
GIVEN `the Minister directs the Authority to grant a licence in a specific case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(9): section 5 prevents the Minister from giving the direction` MEANS
    FALSE
